Cell[BoxData[
    TagBox[\(\[SkeletonIndicator]  Graphics  \[SkeletonIndicator]\),
      False,
      Editable->False]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
at locations (a,0), and (-a,0), two microphone are located.   The microphone \
signals are fed into two logarithmic amplifier, whose output signals (two \
scalars) {v1,v2} serve as input for the net work.  The signal v1 and v2 is \
related to the location {x,y}   by the function v defined below.  First we at \
the distance of microphones from the center a as 0.25.\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(a\  = \ 0.25\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(0.25`\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(v[{x_, y_}]\  := \ {\ \(-\ Log[\ \((x - a)\)^2\  + \ y^2]\), \ \(-\ 
          Log[\((x + a)\)^2\  + \ y^2]\)\ }\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
I.e., the vector v = {v1, v2} is proportional to the distances from the \
source to the microphones.\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell["\<\
We define a function to get sample in such a way so that a point (x,y)is \
distributed in the domain G uniformly. This can be done by first generating \
points uniformly in the rectangle -1 < x < 1, and   0 < y < 0, and simply \
omitting the points outside the domain.\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(usample[]\  := \ 
      Module[\ {x\  = \ 0, \ y\  = \ 2.0}, \[IndentingNewLine]While[
          y\  > \ 1 - \ x^2, \[IndentingNewLine]x\  = \ 
            2.0*Random[]\  - \ 1.0; \[IndentingNewLine]y\  = \ 
            Random[];\[IndentingNewLine]]; \[IndentingNewLine]{x, 
          y}\[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["Let's test output of the usample.", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ListPlot[Table[usample[], \ {10000}]]\)], "Input"],

