}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Let the neural network lattice be L by L.  We set the size here:\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(L\  = \ 15\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(15\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
We initialize the synaptic weight w[[i,j,k]] at random.  Here i and j varies \
over 1 to L, and k = 1 and 2.  That is, neuron {i,j} has two inputs from \
w[[i,j,1]] and w[[i,j,2]].\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(w\  = \ 
        Table[\ usample[], \ {i, \ 1, \ L}, \ {j, \ 1, \ L}];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Some explanation of the notation.  w refers to the hole matrx with index i,j, \
k.   w[[1,1,1]] is an element for the site {1,1} first compoment.  w[[1]] \
refers to the first row of a table each of which is a vector of two \
component.  w[[i,j]] is the synaptic weight associated with [i,j]-th nueron. 
      \
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell["\<\
We define a function that gives a map from v to r = {i,j}. i.e., given the \
input v ={v1,v2}, which neuron fire.  This is obtained by the condition that \
| v - w | is a minimum.  The function distancesquare computes the Euclidean \
distance squared.  The function fire takes a input vector v and the synaptic \
matrix w and computes the smallest distance small and the index {i,j} \
corresponding to the smallest distance.\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(distancesquare[u_, \ 
        v_]\  := \ \((\ u\  - \ v)\)\  . \ \((u\  - \ v)\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(fire[v_List, 
        w_List]\)\(\ \)\(:=\)\(\ \)\(Module[{i, j, small, \ ind, 
          measure}, \[IndentingNewLine]measure\  = \ 
          Map[\ distancesquare[v, \ #] &, \ 
            w, \ {2}]; \[IndentingNewLine]\ \ \ \ small\  = \ 
          Infinity; \[IndentingNewLine]\ \ \ \ ind\  = \ {1, 
            1}; \[IndentingNewLine]For[i\  = \ 1, \ 
          i\  <= \ Length[w], \ \(++i\), \[IndentingNewLine]For[j\  = \ 1, \ 
            j\  <= \ Length[w], \ \(++j\), \[IndentingNewLine]If[\ 
              small > \ 
                measure[\([i, j]\)], \ \ {small, \ 
                  ind\ }\  = \ {measure[\([i, j]\)], \ {i, 
                    j}}]\[IndentingNewLine]]\[IndentingNewLine]]; \
\[IndentingNewLine]{small, \ ind}\[IndentingNewLine]]\)\(\ \ \)\)\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
We know define the step that updates the synaptic strength w according to \
Kohonen's proposal.  That is
w(r)  <- w(r) + epsilon h(r,r') (v - w(r)) .  
h(r,r') is the Gaussian function, for which we first define
\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(h[r_, \ s_, \ sigma_]\  := \ 
      Exp[\ \(-\ distancesquare[r, s]\)/\((2\ sigma^2)\)]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(adaptation[w_, \ v_, \ s_, \ epsilon_, \ sigma_]\  := \ 
      Module[\ {i, j, k, L\  = \ Length[w]}, \[IndentingNewLine]\ 
        Table[\ w[\([i, j, k]\)]\ \  + \ 
            epsilon\ *\ 
              h[{i, j}, s, \ sigma]\ *\ \((\ 
                v[\([k]\)]\  - \ w[\([i, j, k]\)])\), \ {i, \ 1, \ 
            L}, \ {j, \ 1, \ L}, \ {k, \ 1, 
            2}]\[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
We now can put all the functions defined ealier together to get the main \
function.  In the main function, we generate a point unformly in the domain \
G.  The samples are fed to the network for the adaption.  After sufficient \
samples, we plot the w to inspect the results.   In the program below, we \
have commented out the transformation from (x,y) to (v1,v2).\
\>", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(main[nmax_, \ \[Epsilon]0_, \ \[Sigma]0_]\  := \ 
      Module[{vdata, \[Epsilon], \[Sigma], small, \ ind, 
          n}, \[IndentingNewLine]\(Do[\ \[IndentingNewLine] (*\ \(vdata\  = \ 
                  v[usample[]];\)\ *) \[IndentingNewLine]vdata\  = \ 
              usample[]; \[IndentingNewLine]\[Epsilon]\  = \ \[Epsilon]0\ *\ 
                Exp[\ \(-\ n\)/
                    1000.0]; \[IndentingNewLine]\[Sigma]\  = \ \[Sigma]0\ *\ \
\((0.01)\)^\((n/10000.0)\); \[IndentingNewLine]{small, \ ind}\  = \ 
              fire[vdata, \ w]; \[IndentingNewLine]w\  = \ 
              adaptation[w, vdata, 
                ind, \[Epsilon], \ \[Sigma]], \[IndentingNewLine]{n, \ 
              nmax}];\)\[IndentingNewLine]\ \ \[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(draw[w_]\  := \ 
      Show[Graphics[Map[Line, \ Join[w, \ Transpose[w]]]], \ 
        Axes\  \[Rule] \ Automatic]\)], "Input"],

Cell["Intial random w", "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(draw[w]\)], "Input"],

